            <ArticleTitle>Clarence Agress pioneers experimental thrombolysis of the coronary artery in 1952.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>931-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 1952, Clarence Agress performed an experiment on dogs to demonstrate his idea that a thrombus in a coronary artery could be dissolved without harm to the myocardium. Although this landmark in cardiology has been forgotten, credit to Agress is deserved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
